rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0035876237429905643,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":15.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.08764821090348862,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00843370620363966,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.33854,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"FirstSun Capital Bancorp operates as the bank holding company for Sunflower Bank, National Association that provides commercial and consumer banking and financial services to small and medium-sized companies in the United States. It operates through Banking and Mortgage Operations segments. The company offers noninterest and interest-bearing deposit accounts, checking and savings accounts, money market and term certificate accounts, and treasury management products and services, as well as certificates of deposit. It also provides commercial and industrial loans, commercial real estate loans, residential mortgage loans, and small business administration loans, as well as consumer loans, including car, boat, and other recreational vehicle loans. In addition, the company offers residential real estate loans comprising 1-4 family loans, home equity loans, and multi-family loans, as well as credit card accounts, overdrafts, and other revolving loans. Further, it provides remote deposit and cash management products; wealth management services include private banking, wealth planning, investment management, and trust and retirement plan services; and wealth management and trust products, including personal trust and agency accounts, employee benefit and retirement related trust and agency accounts, investment management and advisory agency accounts, and foundation and endowment trust and agency accounts. Additionally, the company offers online banking and bill payment services, online cash management, safe deposit box rentals, and debit card and ATM card services; and packaging and securitization of loans to governmental agencies. It operates through branches in Texas, Kansas, Colorado, New Mexico, Arizona, California, and Washington. The company was formerly known as Sunflower Financial, Inc. and changed its name to FirstSun Capital Bancorp in June 2017. FirstSun Capital Bancorp was founded in 1892 and is headquartered in Denver, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Neal E. Arnold | CEO, President, COO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $264K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $66K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["FirstSun Capital Bancorp is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.8B market cap on $419M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $104M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 34% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Learn Why The Bull Case For FirstSun Capital Bancorp (FSUN) Could Change Following Q3 Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-fsun/firstsun-capital-bancorp/news/learn-why-the-bull-case-for-firstsun-capital-bancorp-fsun-co","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793895991.677,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.893,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"FirstSun Capital Bancorp (NASDAQ:FSUN) Stock Has Consensus Price Target of $45.50","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/firstsun-capital-bancorp-nasdaqfsun-stock-has-consensus-price-target-of-45-50.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793873731.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Financial Contrast: First Community Bancshares (NASDAQ:FCBC) versus FirstSun Capital Bancorp (NASDAQ:FSUN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/financial-contrast-first-community-bancshares-nasdaqfcbc-versus-firstsun-capital-bancorp-nasdaqfsun.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793683725.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"FSUN Q3 deep dive: integration progress and margin gains amid modest revenue miss","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/fsun-q3-deep-dive-integration-010136664.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793667696.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.81,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"33% Below Fair Value Following Q3 Results At FirstSun Capital Bancorp (FSUN)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-fsun/firstsun-capital-bancorp/news/33-below-fair-value-following-q3-results-at-firstsun-capital","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793583133.261,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.954,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Earnings Rebound Could Be A Turning Po